```

## Install OpenCV
Increase swap memory first:

```bash
sudo swapoff -a
sudo dd if=/dev/zero of=/swapfile bs=1G count=8
sudo mkswap /swapfile
sudo swapon /swapfile
grep SwapTotal /proc/meminfo
```

Check Python version:

```bash
python3 --version
```

If using Python 3.9:

```bash
pip3.9 install opencv-python
```

Install required dependencies:

```bash
sudo apt install build-essential cmake git pkg-config libgtk-3-dev
sudo apt install build-essential cmake git pkg-config libavcodec-dev libavformat-dev libswscale-dev libv4l-dev
sudo apt install build-essential cmake git pkg-config libxvidcore-dev libx264-dev libjpeg-dev libpng-dev libtiff-dev
sudo apt install build-essential cmake git pkg-config gfortran openexr libatlas-base-dev python3-dev python3-numpy
sudo apt install build-essential cmake git pkg-config libtbb2 libtbb-dev libdc1394-22-dev
```

Or install them in one command:

```bash
sudo apt install build-essential cmake git pkg-config libgtk-3-dev libavcodec-dev libavformat-dev libswscale-dev libv4l-dev libxvidcore-dev libx264-dev libjpeg-dev libpng-dev libtiff-dev gfortran openexr libatlas-base-dev python3-dev python3-numpy libtbb2 libtbb-dev libdc1394-22-dev
```

Clone OpenCV repositories:

```bash
mkdir opencv_git
cd opencv_git
git clone https://github.com/opencv/opencv.git
git clone https://github.com/opencv/opencv_contrib.git
```

Build OpenCV:

```bash
cd opencv
mkdir cvbuild
cd cvbuild
cmake -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RELEASE \
-D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr/local \
-D INSTALL_C_EXAMPLES=ON \
-D INSTALL_PYTHON_EXAMPLES=ON \
-D OPENCV_GENERATE_PKGCONFIG=ON \
-D OPENCV_EXTRA_MODULES_PATH=~/opencv_git/opencv_contrib/modules \
-D BUILD_EXAMPLES=ON ..
```

Compile:

```bash
make -j4
```

If the system is slow, use:

```bash
make -j1
```

You can check processor cores with:

```bash
nproc
```

Install:

```bash
sudo make install
```

Alternative package installation:

```bash
sudo apt install libopencv-dev python3-opencv
pkg-config --modversion opencv4
```

